{
  "requirement": "The bundled skills MUST direct agents to write site queries that select every place the obligation applies and no others, violation queries for every kind of construct that could break it, and, for every query, `match` and `no_match` snippets that test its conditions.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has three obligations. The bundled skills must direct agents to (1) write site queries that select every place the obligation applies and no others, (2) write violation queries for every kind of construct that could break it, and (3) give every query `match` and `no_match` snippets, violation queries included.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_direct_exact_site_queries_violation_queries_and_snippets]` covers all three. It reads the `## Do` section of the habeas skill's `references/distributed-requirements.md` through the `section` and `distributed_reference` helpers, and `assert_text` checks that each of these phrases is present:\n- Obligation 1: \"check that the site queries select every place the obligation applies and no others\". The source paragraph in `Do` says to check this before the habeas-requirements review, and to widen or narrow the query when it misses or over-selects.\n- Obligation 2: \"Write a violation query, with `within` naming the site query, for every kind of construct that could break the obligation\".\n- Obligation 3: \"Give every query `match` and `no_match` snippets that test its conditions\", plus \"This applies to violation queries too.\" The second phrase covers the violation-query clause.\n\nThis is a documentation-content requirement, so phrase assertions on the guidance text are the appropriate check. The assertions would fail if any directive were removed or weakened, and no other input class or boundary affects the obligations. A search of `assets/skills` for `no_match` and the site and violation query wording found this guidance only in the habeas skill's distributed-requirements reference. No other bundled skill carries it, so testing that file is enough.\n\nThe test has a {test} marker for the subject. There are no acknowledgments and no gaps.",
